From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 06:12:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: apple: pmp-report: release the T8132 GFX
 power request at shutdown

Since the T8132 report pointer is set at probe, a run-time write of
t8132_gfx_request reaches the PMP. A request held that way stays in the
request word through device_shutdown(): the driver's shutdown callback
only stops the J613 floor, and no other path clears the word before a
reboot, a power-off or a kexec. The reboot then restarts the PMP with
the request still set.

Clear the GFX request at shutdown when this driver set or dropped it
before (its bit is known), without waiting for an acknowledgment. A
request bit the driver never wrote is left as it was found, as the
system-sleep path does. Default boots never write the bit, so nothing
changes for them.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
index 9b726b9e07..41a92d7c5f 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
@@ -2566,6 +2566,21 @@ static void apple_pmp_report_shutdown(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	if (rep && rep->j613)
 		j613_floor_stop(rep->j613, "shutdown");
+
+	/*
+	 * A T8132 GFX power request this driver set must not outlive it: a
+	 * reboot restarts the PMP, and nothing tells it the request is gone.
+	 * Clear the bit before the reset, and only if it is ours (a bit this
+	 * driver never wrote is left as it was found, as at a system sleep).
+	 */
+	if (rep && rep->offsets == &apple_pmp_offsets_t8132 &&
+	    (rep->known & BIT_ULL(PMP_T8132_GFX_REQUEST_BIT))) {
+		int ret = apple_pmp_report_set_state(rep, PMP_T8132_GFX_REQUEST_BIT,
+						     false, true);
+
+		dev_info(rep->dev, "t8132: GFX power request (PS-REQ bit %d) released at shutdown: %d\n",
+			 PMP_T8132_GFX_REQUEST_BIT, ret);
+	}
 }
 
 /* System sleep: publish level 0 first, and sample again after resume. */
-- 
